{
  "wasim_version": "0.1.0",
  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "American MAX-CALL on two correlated dividend-paying assets, priced by MULTI-ASSET Longstaff-Schwartz least-squares Monte Carlo. The `lsm` node now takes an extra `states` list; the continuation regression uses a MULTIVARIATE monomial basis of (S1,S2) up to total degree `basis` over in-the-money paths (a single-asset model with empty `states` is byte-identical to before). Two correlated GBM paths (per-step process correlation, rho=0.30) with dividend yield q=0.10 (drift r-q); the dividend is what makes early exercise optimal for a max-call. American price ~9.56 matches a Boyle-Evnine-Gibbs 2-asset binomial lattice at the LSM effective maturity T_eff=T-dt; the European max-call on the same paths is lower by the early-exercise premium. See AMERICAN_OPTION_EXAMPLE.md / AMERICAN_OPTION_SCOPE.md."
  },
